---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
---
<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'API reference',
    description: 'OpenAPI reference for the Backbricks v1 API.',
    tableOfContents: false,
  }}
>
  <p>
    Send requests to your Backbricks deployment under <code>/v1</code>. The reference describes the
    current source build. Your deployment's enabled modules and version determine which operations
    are available.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Public routes accept a project's publishable key in the <code>key</code> query parameter. The
      SDK handles proof of work for browser writes.
    </li>
    <li>
      Server integrations send a scoped secret key as <code>Authorization: Bearer …</code>.
      Operations such as creating a key require a dashboard session.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>To check which modules your deployment has enabled, replace the example host and request its metadata.</p>
  <pre><code>curl https://backbricks.example.com/v1/meta</code></pre>
  <p><a href="/schema/openapi.json">Download OpenAPI JSON</a> · <a href="/docs/errors">Interpret API errors</a></p>
  <div id="api-reference" class="not-content"></div>
</StarlightPage>

<script>
  import { createApiReference } from '@scalar/api-reference';
  import '@scalar/api-reference/style.css';

  createApiReference('#api-reference', {
    sources: [{ url: '/schema/openapi.json', agent: { disabled: true } }],
    telemetry: false,
    layout: 'classic',
    showSidebar: false,
    searchHotKey: 'i',
    withDefaultFonts: false,
    documentDownloadType: 'none',
    hideTestRequestButton: true,
    hideClientButton: true,
    showDeveloperTools: 'never',
    persistAuth: false,
    defaultOpenAllTags: false,
  });
</script>
